                  "The proof states the papers served, the person served, the date, time, address (or place) and manner of service, and facts showing an authorized person served in an authorized manner. For delivery to an individual it describes the person (gender, race, hair color, approximate age, weight, height, other features). For affix-and-mail service it states the dates, addresses and times of the earlier attempts at personal and substituted service. It is a sheriff's or marshal's certificate, a server's affidavit, or the signed CPLR 312-a acknowledgment; a written admission of service by the tenant also suffices.",
                  "(a) Generally. Proof of service shall specify the papers served,", "A writing admitting service by the person to be served is adequate proof of service.",
